  "slug": "clifford-sampling-345a",
  "summary": "Five preprints use classical training, inference or latent search around quantum circuits, covering ground-state samplers, Hamiltonian learning and circuit transfer.",
  "synthesis": "The items share a hybrid pattern in which classical learning machinery trains, guides or designs quantum circuits, and the sampling of noisy circuits is not their central subject. A hypernetwork maps Hamiltonian parameters to circuit angles for ground-state samplers, with shared training and local fine tuning. JEPA-based world models infer Hamiltonian parameters from measured few-body dynamics and recover Ising and Heisenberg chains. QPAT uses a Quantum Circuit Born Machine as a generative prior for classical LSTM, CNN and Transformer training. LatentRL-QAS transfers circuit designs across qubit counts via a circuit VAE and latent-space reinforcement learning. A fully quantum Transformer with non-unitary circuits and training without backpropagation is the most speculative proposal. The common new element is amortizing circuit parameterization or training across tasks rather than optimizing each instance separately.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
